! mcp_bootstrap_p166.strap -- Z FREE, the FREE (release-a-unit)
! routine, printed page 166.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.173,
! header READ and not assumed: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK
! 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID IM000001   DIST. OF 3/01
! 3/01   PAGE NUMBER  166", and the column-heading row's own
! far-right "LOCATION" field is BLANK -- line 1 is an asterisk
! banner that compiles nothing, exactly the rule
! docs/transcription_workflow.md records.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIFTY-SIX PRINTED LINES.  Lines 1-3 are the asterisk banner
! "***** F R E E *****"; lines 4-40 and 50-56 are instructions;
! line 41 is a CNOP that compiles NOTHING (see below); lines 42-45
! and 47-49 are eight entry-mode message/name cells; line 46 is a
! two-word DRZ reservation.
!
!   line   4      Z FREE, the entry.  "BB,S CH OP($10),K K MARK"
!                 -- if the channel is operating, go to K K MARK
!                 (line 50), which saves the IC and goes round the
!                 E LOOP.
!   line   5-6    Z Z FREE: SIC,Z TB RW.32 ; B,Z COM RT.  The
!                 SIC/branch pair is ONE CARD (both lines print
!                 card IM000005).
!   lines  7-13   set S UN ASG, test S P INCL, test bit 2.30($13),
!                 fetch the current reel address, then Z FFLIP
!                 (line 11) clears STATI and dispatches on T REL B
!                 and on bit .26($8).
!   lines 14-16   Z FRE NS / K DFREE: plant "DO NOT SAVE" and set
!                 up the message pointers (LVI,2,Z FRO4 ;
!                 LVI,5,K FRE M).
!   lines 17-23   the owner/entry tests, then SIC,Z ID09X ;
!                 B,Z ID09 "-CONVERT JOB NAME" (one card,
!                 IM000021).
!   lines 24-26   Z FRO6: LVI,7,8. , set S DISPO, and leave to
!                 K UNLD1+1.32.
!   lines 27-36   Z FRO5 / Z FRO5A / Z FRO7: the overlap-reserve
!                 tests, "-REMOVE THE SCRATCH TAPE", and the
!                 preassign-name fetch.
!   lines 37-40   Z F 2 and Z FSAVE: the save path, back to
!                 K D FREE.
!   line  41      CNOP -- see THE CNOP THAT COMPILED NOTHING.
!   lines 42-49   the eight message/name cells the LVIs above point
!                 at, and Z FRO3's two-word DRZ.
!   lines 50-56   K K MARK: V-I,2,.32 ; SV,2,S TIC ; the two
!                 K E LOOP branches; LVI,0,Z Z FREE ;
!                 SV,0,S RET AD($12) ; B,K SUPP.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIFTY-SIX LINES, FIFTY-TWO CARDS, AND NOTHING FELL OFF EITHER END
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SURVEY SAID 30 ROWS, 220245.40..220302.40.  It is short by
! TWENTY-SIX ROWS and stops at line 40 of 56.  The page runs
! 220245.40 .. 220324.40.  Counted off the CARD-SERIAL column, not
! off the survey:
!
!   * line 1 prints card IM000001 and the page header's own
!     "CARD ID IM000001" names it.  The first card of the page is
!     card number ONE, so NOTHING can have fallen off the top.
!     (The header field is the page's FIRST CARD, not a deck
!     prefix: printed p.160's header reads IE000047.)
!   * line 56 prints IM000052.  52 cards + 4 doubled serials
!     (IM000005 on lines 5-6, IM000021 on 22-23, IM000048 on
!     50-51, IM000052 on 55-56) = 56 printed lines exactly, so no
!     line fell off the bottom either.
!   * the counter closes: line 56 is a half-word B,K SUPP at
!     220324.40, so this page LEAVES ITS COUNTER AT 220325.00.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHERE THE COUNTER LEAVES, AND THERE IS NO GAP
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! 220325.00, and the survey puts printed p.167's first row at
! exactly 220325.00.  **The join is contiguous and nothing
! accounts for a gap, because there is no gap** -- the apparent
! 22-word hole between 220302.40 and 220325.00 is entirely the
! survey having stopped reading at line 40.  No reservation and no
! SLC is involved in it.
!
! TWO INTERIOR DISCONTINUITIES, both printed, neither a lost row:
!
!   * line 46, Z FRO3 DRZ(N),(2), prints its COUNT 000002.00 and
!     reserves TWO WORDS, 220311.00 and 220312.00; the next
!     located row is line 47 at 220313.00.  A printed reservation
!     is one of the two legitimate holes.  >>> ITS TRAILING "Z" IS
!     INK ONLY: a reservation prints its count, so no !CHECK on
!     this page or any other can tell DR from DRZ.  Read at 900
!     dpi; recorded as ink.
!   * line 49's datum "PREASSIGN" is NINE characters = 72 bits, so
!     it ends at 220320.08 while line 50 sits at 220320.40.  THAT
!     IS ALIGNMENT, NOT A HOLE -- K K MARK is an instruction and
!     rounds up to the next half word.  Assembled, the 24 bits are
!     part of Z FR17's word; the word count is continuous
!     (220245..220324 inclusive, 48 words, every one touched).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE PAGE DEFINES "ZFRO5" TWICE AND strap_asm REFUSES IT <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIS IS THE ONE THING ON THE PAGE THAT IS NOT SETTLED, and the
! deck below carries a LOUD STAND-IN for it.  What the page prints:
!
!   line 27  220267.00     ZFRO5     BZB,SOVRES($11),ZFRO5A
!   line 30  220272.00  *  ZFRO5     BB,SOVRES($11),ZFRO7
!
! and two references resolve to the TWO DIFFERENT addresses:
!
!   line 18  BZBZ,TMFREJ,ZFRO5   prints 220267.34 04  -> line 27
!   line 20  BB,SOWNER($11),ZFRO5 prints 220272.34 02 -> line 30
!
! MEASURED, NOT EYEBALLED.  Both names were cropped at 1800 dpi at
! identical x and stacked (the cmp2730 method): five glyphs each,
! same cells, Z F R <round> 5, the only difference being that line
! 27's round has dropped ink on its right and line 30's has not.
! Both OPERANDS were cropped the same way: five glyphs each, no
! sixth character on either.  Glyph-ink widths at 1800 dpi, from
! the runs in each row:
!
!   letter O, certain (SOWNER/SOVRES/CONVERT/JOB):  126-135
!   digit 0, certain (same rows' octal fields):     112-126
!   the round in every ZFRO* name and operand:      121-135, mean
!                                                   129 -- LETTER O
!
! so it is not an O/0 split either.  NO READING OF THE INK
! SEPARATES THE TWO SYMBOLS, and no rule I can state produces
! "line 18 takes the first definition and line 20 the second".
!
! WHAT THE DECK DOES.  strap_asm raises
! "line 53: symbol 'ZFRO5' multiply defined" and assembles NOTHING,
! so a failing row is not on offer -- the whole page would be lost.
! Line 30's label and line 20's operand are therefore written
! **ZFRO5DUP**, which is NOT A READING OF ANY GLYPH; both cards
! PRINT "ZFRO5".  Nothing else is changed, the statement and the
! !CHECK agree, and all 44 checkable rows pass.  The alternative --
! dropping line 30's label and letting line 20 compile 220267.34 --
! was rejected because it puts a WRONG WORD in the merged image,
! which is the one thing the workflow says never to do.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CNOP THAT COMPILED NOTHING
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 41 prints "CNOP" with a BLANK LOCATION and a BLANK BINARY
! OUTPUT.  That is the pseudo-op doing its job: line 40 is a
! half-word branch at 220302.40, so the counter is already on a
! word boundary at 220303.00 and no NOP half word is needed.  Line
! 42 prints 220303.00, which is the proof.  It carries no !CHECK
! (there is nothing to check) and no label, and it is the ONLY one
! of the 56 lines that neither a !CHECK nor a !SYM covers.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! COVERAGE -- WHAT IS AND IS NOT CHECKED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! 44 !CHECK rows (lines 4-40 and 50-56) and 22 !SYM symbols.
!
!   * the seven entry-mode DD cells (42-45, 47-49) print NO BINARY
!     OUTPUT, which is the listing behaving normally for entry
!     mode -- but every one of them CARRIES A LABEL, so the !SYM
!     half of check_rows pins all seven to their printed
!     LOCATION.  Do not read their blank binary column as
!     uncovered: the datum lengths are what put the NEXT label on
!     its printed word, and all eight cells' lengths were measured
!     cell-by-cell at 1800 dpi (10 cpi, pitch 180.4 px) rather
!     than counted by eye.  The space after the comma is DATA.
!   * line 46's DRZ carries no !CHECK (a reservation prints its
!     count, not storage; strap_asm renders the storage), as every
!     landed deck with a DR/DRZ does.  Its two words are pinned by
!     K NSAVE arriving at 220313.00.
!   * line 41 is unchecked and nothing about it is unknown.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK -- RECORDED, NOT EXPLAINED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Four rows carry it: lines 15 (220257.00), 30 (220272.00),
! 43 (220306.00) and 46 (220311.00).  Pitches 15, 13 and 3 on a
! 56-line page, which is one more nail in the already-dead
! "fixed physical distance down the form" reading
! (docs/listing_typography.md 12).
!
! ONE HYPOTHESIS RAISED AND KILLED HERE, so nobody spends an hour
! on it: *"it marks a multiply-defined symbol."*  Line 30 is a
! duplicate definition and IS marked, which is why it looked
! promising.  It is refuted by this page's own lines 43 and 46
! (Z FRO4 and Z FRO3 are each defined once and referenced three
! times between them) and conclusively by printed p.3 line 28,
! "BRZ,0.0", which is marked and HAS NO NAME AT ALL.  Make it nine
! things the asterisk is not.
!
! ONE DATA POINT FOR WHOEVER IS STILL COLLECTING THEM, from the
! p.165 render made for the join above: printed p.165 line 35 is
! "220244.00 *  SLC,$" -- a printed SLC,$ that DOES carry the mark,
! on the same side as pp.144/145/147 and against p.151 line 4,
! which does not.  It changes nothing; the universal is already
! refuted.  Recorded so the count is honest.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE EXTERNALS, AND WHERE EACH DATA DESCRIPTION COMES FROM
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every unit-table field below carries the dds of THE PAGE THAT
! PRINTS ITS DEFINING CARD, not one invented here:
!
!   printed p.99's field table  S CH OP .26, STATI .26, S DISPO
!     .27, S UN ASG .29, S SET UP .31, S OWNER .32, S SEL .39,
!     S UN RES .62, S OV RES .63   (decks/mcp_bootstrap_p99.strap
!     lines 181-225)
!   printed p.101  S RET AD 5.0 (BU,19), S C REEL 8.32 (BU,18)
!   printed p.103  S COM RG (8)215001.0 and S P INCL = SCOMRG+.6,
!     which is exactly the 215001.06 line 8 prints.  >>> S COM RG
!     IS WRITTEN AS A SYN STAND-IN, NOT AS p.103's OWN CARD: its
!     defining card is an XW, and copying it would deposit a word
!     at THIS page's counter (the printed p.157 mistake).
!   T REL B 0.27 (BU,1) -- carried by an earlier deck at the same
!     word; this page's line 12 prints 000000.33 88, confirming it.
!
! The absolute externals, each back-derived from a printed
! instruction on THIS page and then CORROBORATED on another page:
!
!   S TIC    (8)215265.0   -- C22-6728 names it (STored Instruction
!                             Counter); eleven landed decks SYN it
!                             at this word.
!   K SUPP   (8)216242.0   -- defined printed p.128, fifteen decks.
!   Z REWST  (8)220226.0   -- line 13's BZB target 220227.34 is
!                             Z REWST+1.0.  Corroborated: the
!                             volume OCR of PDF p.172 (printed
!                             p.165) carries "2  220226.00
!                             220243.40 80  Z REW ST  SIC,Z TB
!                             RW.32" -- a DIFFERENT page, so a
!                             legitimate index, and it is p.165's
!                             first word, which the survey also
!                             gives as 220226.00.
!   Z COM RT (8)220234.40  -- line 6 prints 220234.50 (a B adds
!                             0o10).  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p126
!                             already SYNs it at exactly this.
!   Z TB RW  (8)220243.0   -- line 5's SIC plants 220243.40 for
!                             "Z TB RW.32"; the OCR of printed
!                             p.165 line 24 reads "220243.17 01
!                             LVI,7,Z TB RW", and an LVI,7 adds
!                             0o17 to a .00 address.
!   K E LOOP (8)220374.0   -- lines 52 and 54 both print
!                             220374.34.  SEE THE JOIN FORWARD.
!   Z ID09   (8)221042.0   -- line 23's B prints 221042.10.
!   Z ID09X  (8)221045.0   -- line 22's SIC plants 221045.00.
!   K UNLD1  (8)221751.0   -- line 26's "B,K UNLD1+1.32" prints
!                             221752.50, i.e. target 221752.40.
!                             The OCR of printed p.~202 carries
!                             "27  221751.00  000000.32 88
!                             221752.74 00  K UNLD1  BZB,.-26($8),
!                             $+1.32" -- its own $+1.32 is the SAME
!                             word this page branches to.
!   K SCRAC  (8)222013.0   -- line 29's "L(BU,64),KSCRAC.16" prints
!                             222013.20 (0o20 = 16).  The OCR
!                             carries its defining card on another
!                             page: "24  222013.00  K SCRAC
!                             (IQSX)DD(BU,64),A SCRATCH TAPE XY".
!   T MFREJ  (8)22133.31 (BU,1) -- line 18's first half word prints
!                             022133.31 80.  >>> NO SECOND WITNESS
!                             ANYWHERE: grep of the whole volume
!                             OCR for TMFREJ returns exactly one
!                             hit and it is this page's own card.
!                             See WHAT I COULD NOT SETTLE.
!
! >>> EVERY ABSOLUTE SYN ABOVE IS KNOWN ONLY TO THE HALF WORD.
! Back-derived from a branch or an LVI, bits 0-31 all encode
! identically (workflow, "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE" 1).  The
! ".0" is a convention, not a reading; bit 32 IS checked and all
! of them are on a .00 half word.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN FORWARD -- A FALSIFIABLE PREDICTION FOR p.167
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   1. p.167's first located row is 220325.00, with NO SLC, NO
!      reservation and NO gap: this page's line 56 is a half word
!      at 220324.40.
!   2. p.167's first card is IM000053.
!   3. **p.167 RUNS AT LEAST TO 220374.00**, so the survey's
!      "220325.00..220347.00, 28 rows" is an UNDER-READ as well.
!      The volume OCR of that page carries "32  220374.00
!      000001.45 0D  K E LOOP  V-I,2,1.32" -- K E LOOP's own
!      defining card, the word lines 52 and 54 here both branch
!      to, and it is line 32 of a page the survey stops at row 28.
!      That is one render to falsify.
!   4. p.167 line 32's "V-I,2,1.32" is the same operation as this
!      page's line 50 "V-I,2,.32" one word lower in the value
!      field, so p.166 line 50's 000000.45 0D and p.167 line 32's
!      000001.45 0D check each other.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT I COULD NOT SETTLE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! 1. THE DUPLICATE ZFRO5.  Above, in full.  Unresolved as to
!    MECHANISM; the stand-in is flagged everywhere it appears.
! 2. "Z ID09" vs "Z IDO9" -- DIGIT ZERO OR LETTER O.  The ink
!    leans digit and the deck writes the digit, but say so out
!    loud: the round in "Z ID?9" measures 121 px (line 22) and
!    122 px (line 23) of ink at 1800 dpi, against a same-page
!    digit-0 band of 112-126 (mean 118) and a letter-O band of
!    126-135 (mean 132).  It sits with the digits and BELOW every
!    certain O on the page.  The second, independent line is that
!    the volume OCR shows the series Z ID03, Z ID10, Z ID14,
!    Z ID15, Z ID16 on OTHER pages, which is a numbered series.
!    Neither is proof and the assembler cannot help (both spellings
!    assemble).  If the page that DEFINES it spells it with a
!    letter O, change it here.
! 3. T MFREJ at 022133.31 has NO second witness of any kind -- not
!    a deck, not another page's OCR, not the manuals.  Its word is
!    far below the rest of MCP (0o22133 = 9307), which is unusual
!    enough to be worth re-reading when a "TM" page lands.  Its
!    (BU,1) is inferred from its USE as a branch-on-bit operand,
!    not from a defining card, and a connective taking its length
!    from the symbol is exactly the merge hazard the brief warns
!    about.
! 4. K SCRAC's final glyph.  It is a C or a damaged 0, NOT a D --
!    the left side is round with no vertical stem, which is the
!    workflow's own C/D discriminator.  Four OCR hits on its
!    defining page all read C, but they share this drum, so that
!    is not independent.  "KSCRA0" would be an odd name; C is
!    written.
! 5. Line 44's datum contains a PERIOD: " .  JOB ".  Measured, not
!    guessed -- a 81-px glyph in cell 14, and the datum must be 8
!    characters because Z FRO2 lands on 220310.00.  But 8 blanks
!    would also be 8 characters, so the LENGTH does not prove the
!    period; only the ink does, and the ink is a low 81-px blob
!    that could in principle be a speck.  Nothing on the page
!    distinguishes " .  JOB " from "    JOB " in the binary,
!    because entry mode prints none.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE DECK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

! -- unit-table fields, dds from printed p.99's own table ---------
SCHOP   SYN(BU,1), 0.26             ! p.99 line 22 -CHAN OPERATING
STATI   SYN(BU,1), 0.26             ! p.99 line 23 -TYPE OF TAPE MTED
SDISPO  SYN(BU,1), 0.27             ! p.99 line 25
TRELB   SYN(BU,1), 0.27             ! -REEL LABELED IF ONE
SUNASG  SYN(BU,1), 0.29             ! p.99 line 27 -UNIT ASSIGNMENT
SSETUP  SYN(BU,1), 0.31             ! p.99 line 29 -PSEUDO-OP SET-UP
SOWNER  SYN(BU,1), 0.32             ! p.99 line 30 -PRIORITY LEVEL
SSEL    SYN(BU,1), 0.39             ! p.99 line 32 -SELECT FILE STATUS
SUNRES  SYN(BU,1), 0.62             ! p.99 line 50 -NOT OVERLAP RESERVED
SOVRES  SYN(BU,1), 0.63             ! p.99 line 51 -OVERLAPPED RESERVE
SRETAD  SYN(BU,19), 5.0             ! p.101 line 18 -RETURN ADDRESS IN MCP
SCREEL  SYN(BU,18), 8.32            ! p.101 line 28 -CURRENT REEL ADDRESS

! -- the common region; a STAND-IN, see above ---------------------
SCOMRG  SYN, (8)215001.0            ! p.103 line 8 defines it with an XW
SPINCL  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.6        ! p.103 line 16; line 8 prints 215001.06

! -- absolute externals, bit offset unobservable (half word only) --
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0            ! STored Instruction Counter, C22-6728
KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0            ! printed p.128 "K SUPP NOP,K COMM R"
TMFREJ  SYN(BU,1), (8)22133.31      ! line 18; NO SECOND WITNESS, see above
ZREWST  SYN, (8)220226.0            ! printed p.165's first word
ZCOMRT  SYN, (8)220234.40           ! as p.126's deck writes it
ZTBRW   SYN, (8)220243.0            ! printed p.165 line 24's LVI,7
KELOOP  SYN, (8)220374.0            ! printed p.167 line 32 defines it
ZID09   SYN, (8)221042.0            ! printed "Z IDO9"/"Z ID09", see above
ZID09X  SYN, (8)221045.0            ! printed "Z IDO9X"/"Z ID09X"
KUNLD1  SYN, (8)221751.0            ! K UNLD1's own $+1.32 is 221752.40
KSCRAC  SYN, (8)222013.0            ! "K SCRAC (IQSX)DD(BU,64),A SCRATCH TAPE"

! -- a HARD SLC: this page prints no SLC of its own.  Line 1 is a
! -- banner, so there is no printed "SLC,$" to witness the join,
! -- and a hard origin CANNOT disagree with the arriving counter
! -- (workflow, "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE" 2) -- so printed p.165
! -- WAS COMPARED BY HAND, rendered at 400 dpi here, and it closes:
! --
! --   p.165 has 38 lines, not the survey's 25.  Line 35 prints
! --   "220244.00 *  SLC,$"; lines 36-38 are Z UNLDB's three half
! --   words, and line 38 is "220245.00  221733.10 00  B,K UNLOD".
! --   A half word at 220245.00 LEAVES THE COUNTER AT 220245.40,
! --   which is this page's line 4 exactly.  No gap, no overlap.
! --
! -- p.165 also corroborates two of this deck's externals from its
! -- own ink: its line 28 is "220243.00  220065.50 00  Z TB RW
! -- B,K K LOC" (so Z TB RW = 220243.00) and its line 29 is
! -- "220243.40  220243.50 00  B,$", which is the very half word
! -- this page's line 5 SICs into as "Z TB RW.32".  Its line 37
! -- prints "220234.50 00  B,Z COM RT", character for character
! -- this page's line 6.
        SLC, (8)220245.40

ZFREE   BB,SCHOP($10),KKMARK        ! line  4  printed "S CH OP", "K K MARK"
ZZFREE  SIC,ZTBRW.32                ! line  5  printed "Z Z FREE", "Z TB RW"
        B,ZCOMRT                    ! line  6  same card IM000005 as line 5
        CM1111(BU,1),SUNASG($11)    ! line  7  printed "S UN ASG"
        BB,SPINCL,ZF2               ! line  8  printed "S P INCL", "Z F2"
        BB,2.30($13),ZFSAVE         ! line  9  printed "Z F SAVE" -BRANCH IF SAVE
        LV,8,SCREEL($12)            ! line 10  printed "S C REEL" -GET CURRENT REEL ADDR
ZFFLIP  CM0000(BU,2),STATI($11)     ! line 11
        BZB,TRELB($8),ZFRENS        ! line 12  -BR IF NON- SYSTEM TAPE TO UNLOAD
        BZB,.26($8),ZREWST+1.0      ! line 13
ZFRENS  TI,2,KNSAVE,ZFRO3           ! line 14  printed "Z FRE NS", "K N SAVE", "Z FRO3"
KDFREE  LVI,2,ZFRO4                 ! line 15  printed "K DFREE", "Z FRO4"  (asterisk)
        LVI,5,KFREM                 ! line 16  printed "K FRE M"
        BZB,SOWNER($11),ZFRO5B      ! line 17  -IF PP OWNER
        BZBZ,TMFREJ,ZFRO5           ! line 18  -IF ENRY WAS NOT FROM THE MOVE ROUTINE
ZFRO5B  LVI,7,ZFRO2                 ! line 19  printed "Z FRO5B"
        BB,SOWNER($11),ZFRO5DUP     ! line 20  >>> PRINTS "ZFRO5": see THE PAGE
        LVI,7,ZFRO2                 ! line 21  printed "Z FRO2"
        SIC,ZID09X                  ! line 22  printed "Z IDO9X"
        B,ZID09                     ! line 23  same card IM000021 -CONVERT JOB NAME
ZFRO6   LVI,7,8.                    ! line 24
        CM1111(BU,1),SDISPO($11)    ! line 25  printed "SDISPO"
        B,KUNLD1+1.32               ! line 26  printed "K UNLD1+1.32"
ZFRO5   BZB,SOVRES($11),ZFRO5A      ! line 27  -IF NOT OVERLAP RESERED (sic)
        BB,SUNRES($11),ZFRO7        ! line 28  -IF IT IS NOT OVERLAP RESERVED
ZFRO5A  L(BU,64),KSCRAC.16          ! line 29  -REMOVE THE SCRATCH TAPE
ZFRO5DUP BB,SOVRES($11),ZFRO7       ! line 30  >>> PRINTS "ZFRO5" (asterisk)
        ST(BU,64),ZFRO2             ! line 31
        B,ZFRO6                     ! line 32
ZFRO7   TI,1,ZFR17,ZFRO2            ! line 33
        L(BU,8),ZFR17+1.0           ! line 34  -GET PREASSIGN NAME
        ST(BU,8),ZFRO3              ! line 35
        B,ZFRO6                     ! line 36
ZF2     BB,2.31($13),ZFSAVE         ! line 37  printed "Z F 2" -BRANCH IF SAVE
        B,ZFFLIP-.32                ! line 38
ZFSAVE  TI,2,KSAVE,ZFRO3            ! line 39  printed "Z FSAVE", "KSAVE"
        B,KDFREE                    ! line 40  printed "K D FREE"
        CNOP                        ! line 41  compiles NOTHING; blank location
KFREM   (IQSX)DD(BU), UNLOAD TAPE ON CHANNEL X    ! line 42  24 chars = 3 words
ZFRO4   (IQSX)DD(BU),   UNIT X      ! line 43  8 chars = 1 word  (asterisk)
ZFRO1   (IQSX)DD(BU), .  JOB X      ! line 44  8 chars; the PERIOD is data
ZFRO2   (IQSX)DD(BU),        X      ! line 45  8 blanks = 1 word
ZFRO3   DRZ(N),(2)                  ! line 46  prints 000002.00; Z is INK ONLY (asterisk)
KNSAVE  (IQSX)DD(BU),    DO NOT SAVE X          ! line 47  16 chars = 2 words
KSAVE   (IQSX)DD(BU),       SAVE     X          ! line 48  16 chars = 2 words
ZFR17   (IQSX)DD(BU),PREASSIGNX     ! line 49  9 chars = 72 bits, then alignment
KKMARK  V-I,2,.32                   ! line 50  printed "K K MARK"
        SV,2,STIC                   ! line 51  printed "S TIC"
        BB,SSEL($11),KELOOP         ! line 52  printed "S SEL", "K E LOOP"
        LVI,0,ZZFREE                ! line 53  printed "Z Z FREE"
        BB1,SSETUP($11),KELOOP      ! line 54  printed "S SET UP"
        SV,0,SRETAD($12)            ! line 55  printed "S RET AD"
        B,KSUPP                     ! line 56  printed "K SUPP"; leaves at 220325.00

